  "narration": {
    "title": "June Belonged to Pete Crow-Armstrong",
    "intro": "June is in the books, and this one goes to Pete Crow-Armstrong, who hit like a man playing a different sport. The Cubs outfielder posted a 1.249 OPS with 11 home runs. On the mound, Logan Webb spent the month in a phone booth, allowing almost nothing.",
    "month_hitters_lead": "Crow-Armstrong led all bats in June at 1.249, with Luis Garc\u00eda Jr. close behind at 1.128 for Washington. Shohei Ohtani (1.091) and Junior Caminero (1.075) kept the top of the board loaded, and Dillon Dingler's 1.011 for Detroit was the month's quiet surprise.",
    "month_hr_lead": "Hunter Goodman won the home run count with 13. Crow-Armstrong and Garc\u00eda Jr. tied at 11, and Caminero and Jackson Chourio each cleared 10 \u2014 a busy month for the middle of a lot of lineups.",
    "month_pitchers_lead": "Logan Webb ran the pitching board with a 0.71 ERA in June, barely ahead of Drew Rasmussen's 0.82. Jacob Misiorowski checked in third at 0.96, and Robbie Ray gave the Giants a second name in the top five at 1.36."
  }
